# Line endings: one answer for everyone.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites every file (git's autocrlf turns LF into
# CRLF on checkout), so the first `git status` a contributor sees is 64 modified files
# that they did not touch — and every diff carries the whole file.
#
# `text=auto` normalises on the way in; `eol=lf` keeps the working copy LF, which is what
# the scripts and the tests were written against.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one exception: PowerShell files are read by Windows PowerShell 5.1, whose handling
# of LF-only .ps1 files is a trap this project has already been bitten by.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Anything binary must stay byte-for-byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.apk binary
*.idsig binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
